{#
_boot.html.twig — what opens the setup wizard on its own.

An empty element carrying two controllers: ui--modal supplies the open() the
wizard needs, and onboarding--autostart calls it once. Rendered only while the
user is still pending, so on every other page load this include is a no-op and
nothing reaches the browser.

Size "full" is the max-w-6xl preset in _modal.html.twig — the big modal the
wizard is designed around.

The finish URL and its token ride along because closing the dialog counts as
finishing: setup auto-opens once, and a user who dismisses it has answered.
They can start it again from the user menu.
#}
{% if onboarding.isPending %}
    <div
        data-controller="ui--modal onboarding--autostart"
        data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_onboarding_start') }}"
        data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'onboarding.title'|trans }}"
        data-ui--modal-size-value="full"
        data-onboarding--autostart-finish-url-value="{{ path('app_onboarding_finish') }}"
        data-onboarding--autostart-token-value="{{ csrf_token('onboarding-finish') }}"
        hidden
    ></div>
{% endif %}
